00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.480
Mountains are places where gods are.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.630
As incompetent as I am, they're like my main field of expertise.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.050
Mountains in general are similar to an apparition.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.630
In other words, it's my specialty.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.140
I can understand why they'd want
to put a shrine at the peak, too.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.890
Though, North Shirahebi Shrine and this mountain don't have any connection.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.650
I guess that since two unrelated things
were forcefully tied together, it created discord.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.650
Discord?

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.650
Oh, please disregard that.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.630
Even if there's a mistake in the initial setup,

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.280
it's supposed to be that you can redo
things like that as often as you want.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.410
Are you saying that the shrine being built on this mountain

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.160
was a mistake?

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.180
I...

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.440
came here to repair that mistake.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.060
This is it?

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.860
Yeah, that's it.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.550
This is what Oshino asked me
to come to this spot and attach.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.960
Well, although it's a bit precarious,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.570
it's somehow keeping balance here for the case in question.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.560
The air within the shrine grounds is pretty clear.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.310
Clear, huh?

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.440
Yes.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:17.190
So it's hard to believe this was an energy drift
where bad things gathered, even momentarily.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.910
<i>That's to be expected.</i>

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:24.820
<i>On the last day of summer vacation,
Shinobu and I "cleared" this place, after all.</i>

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.400
But I came here today for a different reason.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.140
What are you doing, Ougi-chan?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.520
<b>SHE'S LIKE A MONKEY, OR A CAT.</b>

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.320
The Snake God is distinctive among them.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.140
Even if you can't call them gods,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.430
snakes are often considered to be sacred.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.640
Do you know why that came to be?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.890
Regarding snakes as sacred?

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:58.150
They aren't a useful animal to humans, such as cows and horses.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.040
It's not that they're commonplace, either.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.650
If you're considering reptiles,
you'd think there'd be other candidates.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.660
Why do you think it was them?

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.180
Why? If I recall...

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.300
That's right.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:14.040
Wasn't it because snakes symbolize immortality or revival?

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.310
Whoa.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.290
You answered correctly right off the bat?

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.060
Snakes grow by molting.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.050
Considering how reclusive an animal the snake is,

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:27.800
you may see the shed skins more often than the snakes themselves.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.870
Well, back when biology wasn't as advanced as it is now,

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.060
if molting of that sort had been observed,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.580
you'd likely regard snakes as sacred beings.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.380
Well, the current problem is settling things in this shrine.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.560
Settling things here in North Shirahebi Shrine,
where a snake that lived over a millennium

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.260
was deified over a millennium ago.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.080
I guess you could say settling what my uncle started, too.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.540
What do you mean?

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.830
The situation involving this place as an energy drift was already resolved, right?

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.090
To make it easy to understand,

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:04.360
the aftermath of the typhoon known as Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade,

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.830
was successfully settled by my uncle.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.280
But I wonder...

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.850
I think that's where my uncle slacked off a bit.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.620
If another apparition at the level of Heart-under-blade were to come,

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.370
I don't think he set up any countermeasures, did he?

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.090
Now that things are safe for the time being,

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:26.880
I believe the next step is to have
countermeasures for the energy drift itself.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.180
If there are no energy drifts,

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.370
there's no way for bad things to pile up.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:37.620
You said this shrine being on this mountain was
a mistake in the initial setup with terrible balance,

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:43.130
but there's nothing a high school girl like you can do about it, is there?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:48.130
We can't just move it somewhere else,
not after all that's happened.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.890
Yes. You're right.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:53.020
Speaking of history, Araragi-senpai,

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:57.220
this shrine, North Shirahebi Shrine,

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.800
used to be in a completely different location.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.050
Completely different?

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:01.690
Yes.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.810
Back then, the name was different, too.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.150
But due to certain circumstances,

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.900
they moved it to this mountain.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.400
They affixed it.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:12.680
At the peak of this mountain,
at the location where I'm standing right now.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.430
There's one thing I'd like you to think about.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.300
How a shrine built somewhere else,

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.420
North Shirahebi Shrine's previous incarnation, which was in another location,

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.750
was relocated to the peak of this mountain by the people back then,

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.420
in other words, those affiliated with this shrine.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.360
How, you ask?

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:37.310
Well, no matter when we're talking about,
it was quite a while ago, right?

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:41.560
Then the building was probably dismantled and brought over.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.440
But Araragi-senpai,

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.460
dismantling it doesn't mean it'll be easy to transport, does it?

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.570
I mean,

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:53.820
back then, paths like the one we climbed up hadn't been made yet.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:04.810
In that case, wouldn't the first step be
to make a path to transport the materials?

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:09.070
This is a lofty, spiritual mountain,
so they can't do such heavy construction.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:12.180
Of course, if you're relocating a shrine to its peak,

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.570
you have to do at least the minimal amount of construction required.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:16.650
What?

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.380
Are you saying they used technology not of this world?

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:22.560
Like some supernatural, or maybe spiritual power?

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.940
If anything, it'd be like a miracle.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.300
No, it's nothing of the sort.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.350
It's merely human wisdom.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:35.200
In my opinion, that's an extremely inconvenient relocation.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.330
Because of that, you could say
that I came here, to this town.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.450
WHITE

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:43.250
Really, what's this White Snake of the North nonsense?

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:43.250
< Shirahebi >

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.240
<i>What you'd call an epilogue, or the punch line for this episode.</i>

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.150
That's so simple, Koyomi-oniichan!

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.510
An easy game!

