Easy game?

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:59.020
There wasn't any elaborate construction like creating a paved road,

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.100
but listening to your story,

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.670
there was at least the minimal amount of construction, right?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.970
Y-Yeah.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.340
So, the people doing the construction,
the ones who finished the project,

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.780
cleared out the land at the mountain peak

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.030
and created the space to build the shrine, right?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:19.990
Yeah. Well, they'd clear the land and create some space.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:22.810
I guess that'd be the minimal amount of construction.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:28.190
And then, you use the trees you chopped down as lumber to build the shrine.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:33.240
That way, you don't have to carry lumber
to the top of the mountain, right?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.820
In other words, there's no need
to make a path just for that.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.740
But Sengoku, they're relocating it, not building a new one.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.100
It's moving the old one.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:47.870
If you built a new shrine using new lumber,
isn't that a completely different shrine?

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:48.910
The corpse —

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:53.610
I mean, the object of worship and things like that would've been brought over.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:58.870
But instead of going to the trouble to relocate,
why not make a brand-new building?

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.210
So they completely swapped buildings
and exchanged one for the other,

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:04.390
then just took the name with them.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:08.880
<i>If there's no change to the faith,
nothing changes even if it's swapped.</i>

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:09.900
<i>No.</i>

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.880
<i>What's important is the balance.</i>

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.540
<i>The act of worshipping a god at the top of that mountain</i>

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.760
<i>is throwing off some sort of balance.</i>

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:18.760
By the way,

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.760
I just thought of something because of that quiz, Koyomi-oniichan.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.990
Well, it wasn't a quiz or anything.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:28.650
That shrine's in ruins, but I wonder if they're going to rebuild it?

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:30.200
Rebuild?

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.280
<i>If that happens, I wonder what will happen
to the balance Ougi-chan's talking about?</i>

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:40.160
<i>Rebuilding a shrine that doesn't have
any visiting worshippers or a god left,</i>

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.660
<i>what kind of faith will be born there by refurbishing it?</i>

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:46.790
<i>No...</i>

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.040
<i>It's not going to be born.</i>

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:49.790
<i>It will continue.</i>

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.830
<i>No matter what the reason is,</i>

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.000
